From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Griffin <christophergriffin05@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 00:40:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 19/66] mac80211: ath11k: don't free a monitor buffer the
 device still holds

ath11k finds a monitor MSDU's buffer by the buf_id in the cookie of the
MSDU link descriptor alone. The device sometimes lists a buffer it handed
back a few milliseconds earlier, whose buf_id the driver has given to a
new buffer since; the driver then frees that new buffer while the device
still holds it, and the device writes a frame into freed memory.

On an Arista C-360 (ipq807x) with a monitor interface on each serving
radio this happened 782 times in 32 minutes (1.75 million monitor
buffers), with mac80211's WARN_ON(!sband) from the garbage this hands
up; on 25.12 the same use crashed the AP several times a day, on
corrupted skb shared info and Ethernet receive buffers.

Add the ath11k patch that checks the buffer address in the link
descriptor against the buffer the cookie names (meant for upstream), and
bump PKG_RELEASE.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Christopher Griffin <christophergriffin05@gmail.com>
---
 package/kernel/mac80211/Makefile              |  2 +-
 ...onitor-buffer-the-device-still-holds.patch | 75 +++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 76 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)
 create mode 100644 package/kernel/mac80211/patches/ath11k/102-wifi-ath11k-don-t-free-a-monitor-buffer-the-device-still-holds.patch

diff --git a/package/kernel/mac80211/Makefile b/package/kernel/mac80211/Makefile
index 1efdf91b7a..87e0f65f1b 100644
--- a/package/kernel/mac80211/Makefile
+++ b/package/kernel/mac80211/Makefile
@@ -12,7 +12,7 @@ PKG_NAME:=mac80211
 
 PKG_SOURCE_VERSION:=7.2
 PKG_VERSION:=$(subst -,_,$(PKG_SOURCE_VERSION))
-PKG_RELEASE:=11
+PKG_RELEASE:=12
 PKG_LICENSE:=GPL-2.0-only
 PKG_LICENSE_FILES:=COPYING
 
diff --git a/package/kernel/mac80211/patches/ath11k/102-wifi-ath11k-don-t-free-a-monitor-buffer-the-device-still-holds.patch b/package/kernel/mac80211/patches/ath11k/102-wifi-ath11k-don-t-free-a-monitor-buffer-the-device-still-holds.patch
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000..ac95b2d89d
--- /dev/null
+++ b/package/kernel/mac80211/patches/ath11k/102-wifi-ath11k-don-t-free-a-monitor-buffer-the-device-still-holds.patch
@@ -0,0 +1,75 @@
+From: Christopher Griffin <christophergriffin05@gmail.com>
+Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath11k: don't free a monitor buffer the device still holds
+
+ath11k_dp_rx_mon_mpdu_pop() finds each MSDU's buffer by the buf_id in the
+cookie of the MSDU link descriptor, and never looks at the buffer address
+beside it. The device sometimes lists a buffer that it handed back a few
+milliseconds earlier. By then the driver has replenished the ring, and
+idr_alloc() has given that buf_id to a new buffer, still posted to the
+device. The driver unmaps and frees that buffer, and the device writes a
+received frame into it later, into memory that belongs to something else
+by then. The duplicate check in ath11k_dp_rx_mon_mpdu_pop() only catches
+the same cookie twice in a row.
+
+On an IPQ8074 with a monitor interface on each radio, the device did this
+about once in 3,600 monitor buffers, e.g.:
+
+  device wrote 0x6ac8d040, handed back 0 ms (3 buffers) earlier as buf_id 1002
+  buf_id 1002 now at 0x709d6e40, still posted to the device
+
+and the AP crashed several times a day, on corrupted skb shared info
+and Ethernet receive buffers.
+
+Take the buffer address from the link descriptor too, and when the
+buffer the cookie names is not at that address, leave it to the device
+and drop the MPDU.
+
+Fixes: d5c65159f289 ("ath11k: driver for Qualcomm IEEE 802.11ax devices")
+Signed-off-by: Christopher Griffin <christophergriffin05@gmail.com>
+---
+--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/hal_rx.h
++++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/hal_rx.h
+@@ -463,6 +463,7 @@ struct hal_rx_msdu_list {
+ 	struct hal_rx_msdu_desc_info msdu_info[HAL_RX_NUM_MSDU_DESC];
+ 	u32 sw_cookie[HAL_RX_NUM_MSDU_DESC];
+ 	u8 rbm[HAL_RX_NUM_MSDU_DESC];
++	dma_addr_t paddr[HAL_RX_NUM_MSDU_DESC];
+ };
+ 
+ void ath11k_hal_reo_status_queue_stats(struct ath11k_base *ab, u32 *reo_desc,
+--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/dp_rx.c
++++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/dp_rx.c
+@@ -4639,6 +4639,11 @@ static void ath11k_hal_rx_msdu_list_get(
+ 		msdu_list->sw_cookie[i] =
+ 			FIELD_GET(BUFFER_ADDR_INFO1_SW_COOKIE,
+ 				  msdu_details[i].buf_addr_info.info1);
++		msdu_list->paddr[i] =
++			((u64)FIELD_GET(BUFFER_ADDR_INFO1_ADDR,
++					msdu_details[i].buf_addr_info.info1) << 32) |
++			FIELD_GET(BUFFER_ADDR_INFO0_ADDR,
++				  msdu_details[i].buf_addr_info.info0);
+ 		tmp = FIELD_GET(BUFFER_ADDR_INFO1_RET_BUF_MGR,
+ 				msdu_details[i].buf_addr_info.info1);
+ 		msdu_list->rbm[i] = tmp;
+@@ -4785,6 +4790,21 @@ u32 ath11k_dp_rx_mon_mpdu_pop(struct ath
+ 				goto next_msdu;
+ 			}
+ 			rxcb = ATH11K_SKB_RXCB(msdu);
++			if (unlikely(rxcb->paddr != msdu_list.paddr[i])) {
++				/* The cookie names a buffer other than the one
++				 * the device wrote, one it still holds: the
++				 * report is stale and the buf_id has been given
++				 * to a new buffer since. Leave that buffer to the
++				 * device and drop the MPDU.
++				 */
++				ath11k_dbg(ar->ab, ATH11K_DBG_DATA,
++					   "msdu_pop: buf_id %d is at %pad, not %pad\n",
++					   buf_id, &rxcb->paddr, &msdu_list.paddr[i]);
++				pmon->rx_mon_stats.dup_mon_buf_cnt++;
++				pmon->mon_last_buf_cookie = msdu_list.sw_cookie[i];
++				drop_mpdu = true;
++				continue;
++			}
+ 			if (!rxcb->unmapped) {
+ 				dma_unmap_single(ar->ab->dev, rxcb->paddr,
+ 						 msdu->len +
